;;;
;;; THE MODEL.  A norm on a vector space E over K is IS-NORM-ON(K, E, nu) (Definition 3.7, CCR-1109-B2
;;; vocabulary ccr-ch3b-vocab): E a module with SCAL(E) the ring view V of K, nu : VEC(E) -> RR,
;;; nu >= 0, nu(x) = 0 iff x = 0, triangle inequality, nu(r x) = |r| nu(x).  "Finite dimensional" is
;;; "has a finite basis": a column u in MAT(n, 1, VEC E) with GENERATES and REL-FREE (mod-seq.scm), the
;;; tree's convention for a free module of rank n.  Coefficients are rows a in MAT(1, n, CARR K), the
;;; vector is LINCOMB(E, n, a, u), and ||a||_max <= c is IS-MAT-BOUND(K, 1, n, a, c) (ccr-ch3-vocab).
;;;
;;; THE THEOREMS.
;;;   ccr-3-8-upper     (K a normed field) for every norm nu and every column u there is C >= 0 with
;;;                     nu(LINCOMB(a, u)) <= C M whenever ||a||_max <= M.  Induction on n with
;;;                     lincomb-row-peel; C = sum_j nu(u_j).
;;;   cn5-row-argmax    a 1-by-n row (n >= 1) has an entry of maximal norm.
;;;   cn5-step          if no c works in the lower bound, then for every k there is a row y with
;;;                     ||y||_max <= 1, an entry of norm 1 and nu(LINCOMB(y, u)) (k + 1) <= 1
;;;                     (y = beta^-1 a, beta an entry of a of maximal norm).
;;;   ccr-3-8-lower     (K a LOCAL NV field, u relation free) there is c >= 0 with
;;;                     |a_j| <= c nu(LINCOMB(a, u)) for every row a and every j.  By contradiction:
;;;                     the rows of cn5-step have a convergent subsequence (ccr-mat-ball-seq-compact,
;;;                     CCR-1109-B3, at 1-by-n), its limit B has nu(LINCOMB(B, u)) = 0 by the upper bound
;;;                     (LINCOMB(B) = LINCOMB(y_k) + LINCOMB(B - y_k)), so B = 0 by REL-FREE, against
;;;                     the entries of norm 1.  n = 0 needs no separate case: the negated bound already
;;;                     supplies an index j in [1, n].
;;;   ccr-3-8-dominate  two norms nu1, nu2 and a basis: nu2 <= C nu1 for some C > 0.
;;;   ccr-3-8-basis     Proposition 3.8 with a given basis: c nu1 <= nu2 <= C nu1, 0 < c, C.
;;;   ccr-3-8           Proposition 3.8: the same for E with SOME finite basis.
;;;
;;; LOAD WINDOW: after theorem-library/ccr-ch3c-ball (ccr-mat-ball-seq-compact) and ccr-ch3c-pb
;;; (cd8-scale-bound, cd8-argmax-nn) of CCR-1109-B3, and structure-library/ccr-ch3b-vocab (IS-NORM-ON,
;;; CCR-1109-B2); everything else it cites (lincomb-*, block-type, entry-of-block, matadd/matscale,
;;; rmm-nn-choice, the rr- and nf- laws) loads earlier.  All of those are unwired on 2026-11-09.

